WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.033
-Welcome back, everybody!
Welcome back!

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:05.133
I'm so happy you're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:06.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
I appreciate you.

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:08.167
Thank you so much.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:10.834
I love this time of year.
Fall is in full swing.

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:12.667
The weather is getting chilly,
which means

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:14.934
it's a great time
to snuggle up with a good book.

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:17.200
And I don't want
you guys reading any bad books.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.467
So to help you out,
I'm going to show you

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.734
some books that
you should avoid at all costs.

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:22.300
That's right -- it's
time for my latest installment

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.868
of my "Do Not Read List."

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:25.267
Here we go.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:26.467
-♪ Do not read ♪

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:27.767
♪ Do not read ♪

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.467
♪ Do not read these books ♪

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:31.467
♪ These books ♪

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.334
-Now, before we start,
I just want you all to know

00:00:33.334 --> 00:00:36.300
that every book that I'm about
to show you is 100% real.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.534
These are actual books.

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:39.100
You can find them on Amazon

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.634
or check them out
at your local library.

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:43.400
They are real.
And don't vote on these.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.968
-Aw.
-These are real books, yeah.

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:47.267
And these are -- Yeah.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:49.133
So, I want to show you
what's on my "Do Not Read List."

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.501
This first one
is a children's book.

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:51.601
-Oh!
-From the '70s, right?

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:53.100
This is very cool.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.934
This one's called "I Want to be
a Service Station Attendant."

00:00:57.934 --> 00:01:01.234
What child doesn't want to be
a service-station attendant?

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:04.100
So, in this story,
the dad gets a flat tire,

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.567
and they pull into
a gas-station attendant

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:08.267
and they meet
this guy named Jim.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:11.634
And then Jim says,
"It's going to take some time."

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:14.634
And the dad says to his son,
"Chuck, do you want to go

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:16.200
across the street
and have a hamburger?"

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.667
And the son says,
"If you don't mind, Dad,

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:20.400
I'd like to stay here
and watch Jim."

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.267
"Dad nodded his head.
'Alright, fine.

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.501
I'll see you both
in a little while.'"

00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:28.133
Take care.
You take care of my kid.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:29.501
-Yeah.

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:32.767
-I'll leave my -- I'm going
to go get that hamburger."

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:36.734
Parenting -- parenting
was different in the '70s.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.567
-Like "Sling Blade."
-It was different in the '70s.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:39.968
"Yeah, just hang out
with that dude."

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:41.801
Oh, check out
this book right here, okay?

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.334
This is a romance book.
-Ooh! I love romance.

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:46.868
-Yeah. This is called
"Will You Give My Mommy a Baby?"

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:48.200
-Oh!

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:52.434
Oh! Oh, wow!

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:55.267
-By Carla Cassidy.
That's kind of a weird title.

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.801
Maybe the art
clears things up down here.

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:57.968
Does it clear anything up?

00:01:57.968 --> 00:02:01.033
No, that's basically saying
what it is, yeah.

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:03.467
Wild.
-Whoa! somebody pitched a tent.

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:05.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.200
-Maybe it's that
gas-station attendant.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.400
-You think it's Jim?
-Jim, yeah.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.133
This next one is a D.I.Y. book.

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.467
-Oh, love it.
-Right?

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:18.601
Everyone loves a do it yourself.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:20.934
Look at this one right here.

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:22.701
There you go.
-You can't say that on TV.

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:26.701
-No, it's a "T" -- "Tucked."

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:28.033
-Oh, "T"!

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:30.501
My bad.
-You thought --

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:31.734
-I thought it was
a different letter.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:34.000
-No, it was not, no.
-Whew!

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.067
-"Tucked --"
It's a quilting book.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:36.501
-Oh, "T" -- tucked, tucked.

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:38.067
-It's a quilting book called...
-"Tucked Up in Bed," yeah.

00:02:38.067 --> 00:02:40.501
-"Tucked Up in Bed."

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:43.501
There's a photo of a couple.
But zoom in on this cover.

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:46.200
Look -- it's like the woman is
laying next to a corpse almost.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.133
-Whoa! Dude, that's tucked up.

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:51.334
-Yeah, that actually is.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:54.167
That's pretty tucked up.
Yeah, I agree.

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:56.100
This next book
is a book about hairstyles.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.267
-Ooh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.267 --> 00:02:59.868
-I love those books.

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:03.334
It's a -- It's called
"Milady's for Men Only."

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:05.601
-Mm!

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:07.634
-Already confusing.

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:09.767
-Milady's.

00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:11.033
-Milady's, yeah.

00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:13.667
But this is the thing
that kind of intrigued me.

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:14.901
I like this.

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:17.400
First of all, I like
this guy's pose right here

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.434
with the glasses.

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:22.100
-Oh, no.
-Oh, hey!

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.534
-Wow!

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:27.701
-But this is --
It's called spot perming.

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:29.100
Anyone know about hair?
Spot perming?

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.234
-Whoo!
-Yeah.

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:32.067
Well, here's the before.

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:33.567
This right here,
if you can zoom in.

00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:35.767
That's before.

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:38.067
And here's the after.

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:41.667
He's basically just -- He just
faced a different direction.

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:44.467
-Yeah.
-That's the before and after.

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:46.167
Why mess with perfection?

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:47.734
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:49.000
-This next book -- I love this.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.601
It's called
"Disguise Techniques."

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:52.701
"Disguise Techniques."

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:55.734
Yep. And it says,
"Nothing more to disguise

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:57.868
than putting on a costume."

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.434
So, let's see a costume,

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:02.033
the disguise techniques
they tell you here.

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:03.767
Alright, so,
this is really good.

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:06.067
This is an illustration
to help you out here.

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:07.801
This is a real book.
Look at the bottom one first.

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:10.767
This is normal people just
waiting for at bus stop, right?

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:12.100
Once you put on
a little disguise,

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.567
no one will even notice
that you're at the bus stop.

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:17.934
No one will even notice.
-No.

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:19.234
"What's that?"
"Nothing."

00:04:19.234 --> 00:04:22.400
-Nothing.
It's a clown next to a hippie.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.901
-Next to a flapper.
Yeah, nobody knows nothing.

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:24.968
-A flapper.

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:26.234
People are just
waiting for a bus.

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:27.334
-Yeah.
-What's the problem?

00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:30.501
-Yeah.
"What are you talking about?"

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:33.300
"I don't notice anything, yeah.
Why would my eye go there?"

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.734
-My eye would not go there.
-No, it would go right past it.

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:37.501
-Yeah, right to the bus, yeah.
-Yep. Right on the bus.

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:39.901
-Yeah, no, those people
waiting for the bus --

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:41.534
"What's going on?

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:43.501
I'm getting a little --
But now it's a clown.

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:45.267
And now I get it."

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:46.667
This -- We're down to
our last book here.

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:52.400
This is called
"Religion, Philosophy and Fun."

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.167
Can we see the author?

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:55.601
Looks like he's
having a blast right there.

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:56.667
There he is -- Bud Robinson.

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.367
That's all we have for
"Do Not Read."

00:04:58.367 --> 00:05:00.734
If you have a book you think
should be on our list,

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:03.133
send it to
donotread@tonightshow.com.

